<content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    Explain what it means to factor a polynomial completely.
    <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> To factor a polynomial completely means that every factor you have found, or the polynomial itself, is prime.
  </item>
</list>
<para>For questions 2 - 7, determine if each polynomial is completely factored. If the answer is no, write the completely factored form.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    \(3x(8x^2 − 9x − 3)\)<emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>yes
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>\(
    60x^2y − 75xy + 30y\)
    <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>no;</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    \(2c(4c^2 + 20cd + 81d^2)\)<emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>yes
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    \(5n^2 + 5n + 12\)<emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> yes
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    \(5q^2 − 15q − 90\)
    <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> no;</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>
    \(64x^2 + 16xy + y^2\)<emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>no;</item>
</list></section>
</content>
